<!-- The Insights app's context (impl-insights §2, P1; design-insights §1.1, §15.2; Insights.js): the organizations whose results
    the user sees, the capabilities from the INSIGHTS_* permissions, safe defaults and the canonical links. A user may open Insights
    through an authorization of their groups on its root (BOSS_INSIGHTS, the root user group, or BOSS_INSIGHTS_ADMIN); the root
    grant opens navigation only. The report engine checks its own artifacts whatever this answers: a capability opens an
    affordance, never a source. Disabled artifact authorization widens nothing here. P4 adds search#Records, the palette's
    dashboards and saved reports (Registry.js); P10 adds get#Settings and store#Settings, the organization's analytics defaults
    (Settings.js; design §11 Settings). -->
<services xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/service-definition-3.xsd">
    <service verb="get" noun="Context" allow-remote="false">
        <description>Check that the user may open Insights and resolve their context: the capabilities (the INSIGHTS_* permissions
            and whether the copied report screens open), the organization choices (theirs, or every internal organization for the
            Insights administrator with none active), the organization in scope (the requested one, else the active one, else the
            only one), the safe defaults (a relative reporting range, currencies kept apart), the canonical links and the
            framework report screens' links and policy under Insights (reportLinks, with no editor for a user who does not
            author; reportPolicy, what Insights' own services do, as data for the screens: the default range, who may set an
            alert or share, the fixed parts of a dataset, a schedule and an alert, the organization's calendar). Refuses a
            user without Insights (INSIGHTS_UNAVAILABLE), a Projects client contact and a PASS public account among them, another
            app root (INSIGHTS_CONTEXT) and an organization that is not the user's, existing or not (ORGANIZATION_UNAVAILABLE).</description>
        <in-parameters>
            <parameter name="appRoot"/>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
        </in-parameters>
        <out-parameters>
            <parameter name="capabilities" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="organizations" type="List"/>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyIds" type="List"/>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
            <parameter name="allOrganizations" type="Boolean"/>
            <parameter name="defaults" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="appRoot"/>
            <parameter name="sharedLinks" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="reportLinks" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="reportPolicy" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="linkBase"/>
            <parameter name="webBase"/>
        </out-parameters>
        <actions>
            <set field="module" value="component://mr-boss/service/ironstone/insights/Insights.js"/>
            <set field="found" from="ec.resource.script(module).execute('context', context)"/>
            <set field="capabilities" from="found.capabilities"/>
            <set field="organizations" from="found.organizations"/>
            <set field="organizationPartyIds" from="found.organizationPartyIds"/>
            <set field="organizationPartyId" from="found.organizationPartyId"/>
            <set field="allOrganizations" from="found.allOrganizations"/>
            <set field="defaults" from="found.defaults"/>
            <set field="appRoot" from="found.appRoot"/>
            <set field="sharedLinks" from="found.sharedLinks"/>
            <set field="reportLinks" from="found.reportLinks"/>
            <set field="reportPolicy" from="found.reportPolicy"/>
            <set field="linkBase" from="found.linkBase"/>
            <set field="webBase" from="found.webBase"/>
        </actions>
    </service>
    <service verb="get" noun="DeliveryPolicy" allow-remote="false">
        <description>What an area of Insights that delivers adds to the root's reportPolicy for the framework's report screens it
            shows (Scheduled reports; mr-moqui docs/tools/Monitoring.md, "Mounting the report screens"): recipientCap, the most
            recipients a group delivery is saved and checked with, the cap of the organization the caller works in (else the
            lowest of the organizations in their scope), never above the instance ceiling. It is read where it is used, not by
            get#Context for every request. Refuses a user without Insights (INSIGHTS_UNAVAILABLE).</description>
        <out-parameters><parameter name="recipientCap" type="Integer"/></out-parameters>
        <actions>
            <set field="found" from="ec.resource.script('component://mr-boss/service/ironstone/insights/Insights.js').execute('deliveryPolicy', context)"/>
            <set field="recipientCap" from="found.recipientCap"/>
        </actions>
    </service>
    <service verb="search" noun="Records" allow-remote="false">
        <description>The palette's Insights rows (design §1.2): the user's saved dashboards and reports and the shipped business
            dashboards whose title matches, each with recordEntity, recordId and its link. No rows for a user without Insights
            read.</description>
        <in-parameters>
            <parameter name="text"/>
            <parameter name="limit" type="Integer"/>
            <parameter name="docTypes" type="List"/>
            <parameter name="idMatch" type="Boolean"/>
        </in-parameters>
        <out-parameters>
            <parameter name="rows" type="List"/>
        </out-parameters>
        <actions>
            <set field="found" from="ec.resource.script('component://mr-boss/service/ironstone/insights/Registry.js').execute('searchRecords', context)"/>
            <set field="rows" from="found.rows"/>
        </actions>
    </service>
    <service verb="get" noun="Settings" allow-remote="false">
        <description>Insights' settings for the organization in scope (design §11 Settings): for every Insights reader the
            controls in effect, in words (the fiscal calendar, which is Accounting's; the display zone and week; delivery
            modes and who may schedule; the group recipient cap under the instance ceiling; export and retention limits;
            the freshness policy), and for a holder of INSIGHTS_SETTINGS_VIEW the organization's analytics defaults (the
            registered PartySetting types) with their revision, the choices and the source owners (each registered source's
            domain owner, class, admission state and steward; no data). Refuses a user without Insights
            (INSIGHTS_UNAVAILABLE) or without Insights read (INSIGHTS_VIEW_REQUIRED) and an organization that is not the
            user's (ORGANIZATION_UNAVAILABLE).</description>
        <in-parameters>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
        </in-parameters>
        <out-parameters>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
            <parameter name="organizationName"/>
            <parameter name="organizations" type="List"/>
            <parameter name="canView" type="Boolean"/>
            <parameter name="canEdit" type="Boolean"/>
            <parameter name="recipientCeiling" type="Integer"/>
            <parameter name="controls" type="List"/>
            <parameter name="settings" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="revision"/>
            <parameter name="options" type="Map"/>
            <parameter name="sources" type="List"/>
        </out-parameters>
        <actions>
            <set field="found" from="ec.resource.script('component://mr-boss/service/ironstone/insights/Settings.js').execute('getSettings', context)"/>
            <set field="organizationPartyId" from="found.organizationPartyId"/>
            <set field="organizationName" from="found.organizationName"/>
            <set field="organizations" from="found.organizations"/>
            <set field="canView" from="found.canView"/>
            <set field="canEdit" from="found.canEdit"/>
            <set field="recipientCeiling" from="found.recipientCeiling"/>
            <set field="controls" from="found.controls"/>
            <set field="settings" from="found.settings"/>
            <set field="revision" from="found.revision"/>
            <set field="options" from="found.options"/>
            <set field="sources" from="found.sources"/>
        </actions>
    </service>
    <service verb="store" noun="Settings" allow-remote="false">
        <description>An organization's analytics defaults (design §11 AnalyticsDefaults), the registered PartySetting types
            mr-boss seeds: the default dashboard, flow map and digest (each one the saver reads), the display time zone and
            week start, the freshness policy and the recipient cap of group delivery. An empty choice stays empty; fiscal
            periods are Accounting's and are not set here. Needs INSIGHTS_SETTINGS_EDIT (INSIGHTS_SETTINGS_REQUIRED) for an
            organization in the caller's scope (ORGANIZATION_UNAVAILABLE), at the revision read (SETTINGS_CHANGED); a value
            outside its choices is refused (VALUE_INVALID) and a cap above Admin's instance ceiling too
            (RECIPIENT_CAP_CEILING): an app form never raises an instance limit. A refusal is the answer (applied false
            with reasonCode and reason).</description>
        <in-parameters>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
            <parameter name="defaultDashboardId"/>
            <parameter name="defaultMapId"/>
            <parameter name="defaultDigestDefinitionId"/>
            <parameter name="displayTimeZone"/>
            <parameter name="weekStart"/>
            <parameter name="freshnessPolicyId"/>
            <parameter name="groupRecipientCap"/>
            <parameter name="expectedRevision"/>
        </in-parameters>
        <out-parameters>
            <parameter name="applied" type="Boolean"/>
            <parameter name="reasonCode"/>
            <parameter name="reason"/>
            <parameter name="organizationPartyId"/>
            <parameter name="changedCount" type="Integer"/>
            <parameter name="revision"/>
            <parameter name="settings" type="Map"/>
        </out-parameters>
        <actions>
            <set field="found" from="ec.resource.script('component://mr-boss/service/ironstone/insights/Settings.js').execute('storeSettings', context)"/>
            <set field="applied" from="found.applied"/>
            <set field="reasonCode" from="found.reasonCode"/>
            <set field="reason" from="found.reason"/>
            <set field="organizationPartyId" from="found.organizationPartyId"/>
            <set field="changedCount" from="found.changedCount"/>
            <set field="revision" from="found.revision"/>
            <set field="settings" from="found.settings"/>
        </actions>
    </service>
</services>
